From 593763a41b0c29475b14cee7e3e069d49c2d5a30 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:50:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/70] ppc-darwin: define __STDC_FORMAT_MACROS where the C99
 format macros are used

G5 build error #6 of the 12.4 port (v8_base, incremental-marking.cc:
PRIi64 undeclared).  The PowerPC-era Mac OS X SDK gates the C99 PRI*
macros for C++ behind __STDC_FORMAT_MACROS, and the define only works
if it precedes the first - possibly transitive - inclusion of
<inttypes.h>; a bare #include <inttypes.h> (which the failing file
even has) exposes nothing.  Files that go through libstdc++'s
<cinttypes> are fine (the 9.4-era convention carried in patch 0025,
G5-validated across whole builds), which the sweep confirms
empirically: every already-compiled PRI user in this build has a
direct <cinttypes>.

Class sweep of the whole tree (grep for non-V8PRI* C99 macro uses,
filtered to TUs compiled on this target): the unprotected set is
incremental-marking.cc, the embedded-file-writer base and win TUs
(the win writer compiles on every host), wasm-code-manager.cc and
wasm-objects.cc, plus two wasm headers - function-body-decoder-impl.h
and module-decoder-impl.h - whose PRI uses compile inside their
includers, so the whole consumer closure (via wasm-disassembler-impl,
constant-expression-interface and turboshaft-graph-interface) gets
the guard too: factory, module-decoder, constant-expression{,-interface},
{function-body,graph-builder}-decoder/interface, function-compiler,
liftoff-compiler, turboshaft-graph-interface, wasm-disassembler,
wrappers and compiler/pipeline.  module-instantiate keeps its 0025
<cinttypes>.  Non-issues verified: V8PRIxPTR/V8PRIdPTR are V8's own
string-literal macros (deoptimizer, translated-state, assembler-ppc -
all already compiled); disassembler.cc's uses are ENABLE_DISASSEMBLER-
gated; simulator/other-arch/gdb-server TUs are not compiled; the absl
closure's two PRI users built long ago.

One uniform guarded define block at the top of each file, before any
include - a no-op on modern SDKs and glibc, which define the macros
unconditionally.

13.6 rebase: graph-builder-interface.cc no longer exists upstream (its hunk is dropped); the other files only needed their guard block re-placed ahead of 13.6's new first lines.

13.6 parade #7 (2026-10-27): translated-state.cc and deserializer.cc
are new PRI users at 13.6 (12.4 only used V8's own V8PRIxPTR there;
13.6 prints the wasm int64/double deopt literals with PRId64/PRIx64
and deserializer addresses with PRIxPTR), each with a bare
Both get the guard block.  The sweep was redone as an include-order
simulation over the harness's 908 ppc TUs (other-arch headers pruned;
the out-of-tree ICU public headers and the in-tree simdutf, highway
and fast_float headers checked: none includes <inttypes.h> without
<cinttypes>): these two are the only unprotected PRI uses, every other
compiled PRI user reaches <cinttypes> before any raw <inttypes.h>.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
